{{- /*
=============================================================================
configure-pi-theme — idempotent ~/.pi/agent/settings.json theme patcher

Pi (the @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent open-source AI coding harness) loads
its theme selection from ~/.pi/agent/settings.json. That file is NOT fully
owned by the repo — pi writes runtime keys (defaultProvider, defaultModel,
defaultThinkingLevel, lastChangelogVersion) and the user edits it interactively
via /settings. A templated file target would clobber those keys; this jq merge
preserves every existing field and only sets the `theme` scalar to
`tokyo-night-moon` (the custom theme deployed by dot_pi/agent/themes/).

Uses `run_onchange_before_` semantics:
  • `onchange_` runs only when THIS SCRIPT'S source content has changed
    (chezmoi state hash), so re-applies don't churn ~/.pi/agent/settings.json's
    mtime once the patch is stable.
  • `before_` runs during step 4 of the application order, before file
    targets are written — matters because ~/.pi/agent/settings.json is NOT
    a chezmoi-managed file; this script is the only writer for the `theme`
    key. The theme JSON file (dot_pi/agent/themes/tokyo-night-moon.json) is
    written in step 5 as a normal chezmoi file target; the ordering here only
    matters relative to other run-scripts that might read this file's output.

No-op on a fresh machine where pi has never been run (the ~/.pi/agent/ dir
won't exist yet — pi creates it on first launch). The user runs `pi` once to
initialize, then re-runs `chezmoi apply` to apply the theme selection. This
is the same friendly-fail-mode pattern AGENTS.md describes for dot_zprofile
on a machine where brew isn't installed yet.
=============================================================================
*/ -}}
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" -}}
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

PI_DIR="$HOME/.pi/agent"
SETTINGS_FILE="$PI_DIR/settings.json"

# No-op if pi has never been run (dir or settings file doesn't exist).
if [ ! -f "$SETTINGS_FILE" ]; then
  echo "==> Pi settings not found at $SETTINGS_FILE — pi not initialized yet."
  echo "    Run 'pi' once to initialize, then re-run 'chezmoi apply' to select the theme."
  exit 0
fi

echo "==> Selecting Tokyo Night Moon theme for pi (~/.pi/agent/settings.json)..."
tmp=$(mktemp)
jq --arg theme "tokyo-night-moon" '.theme = $theme' "$SETTINGS_FILE" > "$tmp" && mv "$tmp" "$SETTINGS_FILE"
echo "    theme = tokyo-night-moon (other keys preserved)"
{{- else -}}
{{- /* No-op on non-macOS. */ -}}
{{- end -}}